<task id="102" project="email-communication-solution-r4">
  <metadata>
    <title>Association Engine — contact-name matching in subject/body (Suggest-only) (UAT R2 B1)</title>
    <phase>Wave 10 — UAT round 2 refinements</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>5</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>015,091</dependencies>
    <blocks>—</blocks>
    <tags>bff-api, communication</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Adds an Association Engine capability (a rung / deterministic matcher); BFF-touching; correctness + precision-sensitive. Code-review + adr-check.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W10</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <fr-refs>FR-10</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    UAT round 2 B1 (`notes/UAT-ROUND2-FEEDBACK.md`): an email whose BODY named two contacts already in the system
    ("Working on this file will be Eyal Iffergan and Sara Chen") did NOT surface them. Today contacts match ONLY
    when they are the sender/recipient (ParticipantCorrelationRung / rung 2). Owner wants contacts NAMED in the
    subject/body to surface too.

    OWNER DECISION (2026-07-20): contact-name matches are SUGGEST-ONLY — surface for the reviewer to confirm,
    never auto-file. (This is structurally guaranteed regardless: `sprk_regardingperson` is a FALLBACK field in
    `AssociationStatusMapper` — a contact match never auto-files by itself. So emitting these matches cannot change
    auto-file behavior.)

    Add deterministic contact-name matching over the normalized envelope (subject + body + attachment text):
    extract candidate PERSON-NAME tokens (a run of 2+ capitalized name tokens), resolve them by EXACT full-name
    lookup against `contact` records (fullname / firstname+lastname), and emit `sprk_regardingperson` matches at a
    Suggested-band confidence. Precision guards are ESSENTIAL — a single common name is far too weak; require a
    2-token (first + last) match against an existing contact, and gate on a minimum length. Mirror the retrieve/
    verify discipline + precision guards of `RecordNameMatchRung` (rung 3.5), but for contacts (which are NOT in
    the records index — use a Dataverse contact query).
  </prompt>

  <goal>
    A contact already in the system, named by full name in the subject/body, surfaces as a Suggested
    `sprk_regardingperson` candidate (the reviewer confirms/dismisses — matching the C1 "Suggested" section). No
    auto-file behavior change; the mapper/ladder are unchanged; precision guards prevent common-name false matches.
  </goal>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The engine extracts candidate full-name tokens (≥2 capitalized tokens) from subject + body + attachment and resolves each by exact full-name match against existing `contact` records.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A matched contact emits a `sprk_regardingperson` `RungMatch` at a Suggested-band confidence (below the auto-file threshold; and the field is a mapper fallback → never auto-files) with provenance naming where it matched (subject/body/attachment).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Precision guards: a single-token name, or a name that resolves to NO contact, emits nothing. Covered by unit tests (e.g. "Sara" alone → no match; "Sara Chen" matching a contact → match; "Sara Chen" matching no contact → no match).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The email-1 scenario: body "Eyal Iffergan and Sara Chen" (both existing contacts) → two Suggested `sprk_regardingperson` candidates. Regression test (ADR-038 KEEP-path, boundary-mocked contact lookup).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No auto-file behavior change (contact is a fallback field); `AssociationStatusMapper` untouched. Existing 516 Communication tests still green.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">§10: publish-size + delta (≤60) reported; no new HIGH CVE; §11 Placement Justification (extend engine; reuse/extend `ICommunicationDataverseService` for the contact query — no new service unless genuinely absent).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <constraints>
    <constraint>Envelope-only (ADR-045) — never `Microsoft.Graph.Message`.</constraint>
    <constraint>Reuse/extend `ICommunicationDataverseService` for the contact-by-name query (add a method there if none exists, justified ≤2 sentences) — do NOT add a new service (§11). Contacts are NOT in `spaarke-records-index`, so this is a Dataverse query, not a RecordSearch call.</constraint>
    <constraint>Suggest-only: do NOT add `contact` to the mapper's auto-file-eligible set; do NOT change the ladder.</constraint>
    <constraint>Best-effort/non-fatal (NFR-06); regex extraction bounded with a timeout (mirror RecordNameMatchRung / ExplicitReferenceRung).</constraint>
    <constraint>Register any new rung as a concrete `IAssociationRung` singleton (ADR-010), self-gated by an `Enabled` kill-switch bound via IOptionsMonitor (parity with rungs 3.5/4/5).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <notes>
    Design choice for the implementer: a NEW deterministic rung (e.g. `ContactNameMatchRung`) mirroring
    `RecordNameMatchRung`'s structure is the cleanest fit (records-index rung can't serve contacts). Confirm the
    contact query surface on `ICommunicationDataverseService`; ParticipantCorrelationRung already queries contacts
    by email — extend that Dataverse client with a by-name query. Common-name false-positive risk is the main
    design hazard — bias toward precision (full-name exact match) over recall.
  </notes>
</task>
